## Contracts on Method Definitions

```xiom
pub type Stack = { items: Vec[Int]; }

impl Stack {
  fn push(self: &mut Self, item: Int)
    ensures: self.len() == self@pre.len() + 1;
  { self.items.push(item); }

  fn pop(self: &mut Self) -> Int
    requires: self.len() > 0;
    ensures: self.len() == self@pre.len() - 1;
  { return self.items.pop(); }

  fn len(self: &Self) -> Int { return self.items.len(); }
}
```

### self@pre in Methods
`self@pre` refers to the object's state BEFORE the method executed:

```xiom
impl Counter {
  fn increment(self: &mut Self) -> Int
    ensures: self.value == self@pre.value + 1;
    ensures: result == self.value;
  {
    self.value = self.value + 1;
    return self.value;
  }
}
```

### Methods with Invariants
When a type has an invariant, every method must maintain it:

```xiom
pub type PositiveStack = Stack
  invariant: self.len() >= 0;

impl PositiveStack {
  fn clear(self: &mut Self)
    ensures: self.len() == 0;
  { self.items.clear(); }  // Invariant: 0 >= 0 ✓
}
```

